# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MentorHer backend — Docker Compose environment (copy to ".env" and edit)
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Values in .env are used for Docker Compose VARIABLE INTERPOLATION
# (RabbitMQ container login + host ports) and are also passed to the
# web/worker containers as environment variables.
#
# App secrets can alternatively live in ".env.local" (same keys as plain
# dev outside Docker). If both files define the same key, .env.local wins.
# Do NOT commit either file (both are gitignored).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- RabbitMQ (containers use this login; guest/guest is refused off-localhost) ---
# Use letters/digits only — the password goes inside a URL.
RABBITMQ_USER=mentorher
RABBITMQ_PASSWORD=change_me_strong_password

# --- Secrets for the web + worker containers ---
# (a real .env.local with these values also works and takes precedence)
JWT_SECRET=change_me_long_random_string
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: MongoDB for compose (defaults to the in-stack mongo container) ---
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb://mongo:27017/mentorher

# --- Optional host ports (defaults shown) ---
# FRONTEND_PORT=3000
# BACKEND_PORT=3001
# RABBIT_UI_PORT=15672

# --- Extra browser origins allowed by the API's CORS middleware ---
# Comma-separated. Needed when the frontend runs on a non-default host port,
# e.g. FRONTEND_PORT=3005 -> CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3005,http://127.0.0.1:3005
# (Vercel + localhost:3000 are always allowed without this.)
# CORS_ORIGINS=

# --- Optional: frontend build-time variables (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) ---
# Same values as mentorher-frontend/.env.local (they are public in the client bundle).
# Changing them requires: docker compose build frontend
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=
